---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import AspectRatioDemo from '../../components/AspectRatioDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Aspect Ratio"
  description="A frame that keeps images, video, and placeholders at a fixed width-to-height ratio."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Aspect Ratio</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Keeps content at a fixed shape as its width changes. Use it for images, video, and the placeholders that hold their
    space.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <AspectRatioDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Aspect Ratio usage"
      code={`import { AspectRatio } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/aspect-ratio";

<div className="w-full max-w-72 overflow-hidden rounded-xl">
  <AspectRatio ratio={16 / 9}>
    <img
      src="/landscape.svg"
      alt="Fictional green landscape"
      className="size-full object-cover"
    />
  </AspectRatio>
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>ratio</code> is required. It is width divided by height, so
      <code>16 / 9</code>, <code>4 / 3</code>, and <code>1</code> give wide, photo, and square frames. The frame takes
      the full width it is given and sets its height from the ratio. Content taller than the frame does not stretch it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The frame is a <code>div</code> with <code>position: relative</code> and
      <code>data-slot="aspect-ratio"</code>. It takes all <code>div</code> props.
      <code>className</code> and <code>style</code> merge with its own, and the ratio is set as{' '}
      <code>--sprout-aspect-ratio</code>. Make children fill it with <code>size-full</code>, or place them with{' '}
      <code>absolute inset-0</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The frame does not round or clip. Wrap it, or pass <code>className</code>, with <code>overflow-hidden</code> and a
      radius when the corners should be round.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Aspect Ratio adds no role and no focus stop. Give images real
      <code>alt</code> text. While content loads, put <code>aria-busy</code> on the frame and a{' '}
      <code>role="status"</code> placeholder inside it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
